                  "title": "Holiday Calendar & Observance",
                  "section": "5.1",
                  "section_heading": "Remembrance Day (Toronto)",
                  "text": "On November 11 the Toronto office observes two minutes of silence at 11:00. Remembrance Day is a regular working day for the Toronto office, not a company holiday, so a Toronto employee taking PTO on November 11 is charged a PTO day for it. (For the US offices, November 11 is Veterans Day, a company holiday; see \u00a72.)\nToronto colleagues working with US teams that week should expect the US offices to be closed on November 11, and US staff should not assume their Toronto colleagues are off. Staff of any office who wish to join the Toronto observance remotely are welcome to do so.",
